meta {
  name: Session scripted route
  type: http
  seq: 43
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sim/routes/:sessionId
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  sessionId: 229
}

docs {
  200 { runId, sessionId, deviceId, startMs, gunMs, durationSec, points:[{t,lat,lon}] }
  400 { error }  // sessionId not a number (param unresolved)
  404 { error }  // no persisted route for this session

  The scripted route the mock boat sailed for this SESSION, keyed by session
  rather than by run id.

  Set a real session id in the path param: ids are autoincrement, so they do not
  restart at 1 (the 2026-10 DB rewrite left the live sessions at 196+). A stale
  id answers 404 "no scripted route for this session" — that is the route being
  right, not the request.

  Keyed by session on purpose: the frontend only holds a selected session id,
  so /sim/runs/:id/points is unreachable exactly when it is needed. A run is
  pruned 10 minutes after it ends, and mock uploads never reach gps_points,
  so a FINISHED session used to have no track to draw at all.

  Serves the persisted route, so it also works across a backend restart.
  points are downsampled 1:5 with the last sample always included.
}
